## Usage

{% if output_mode == 'terraform' %}
Run `terraform init`, `terraform plan`, and `terraform apply` from this repository root.
{% if backend == 'datadog' %}
The Datadog provider sets `validate = false` so `terraform plan` works in CI and portal dry-run
without `DD_API_KEY` / `DD_APP_KEY`; live apply still requires credentials.
{% elif backend == 'prometheus' %}
Prometheus Terraform mode stores rule groups and Alertmanager YAML in `null_resource` triggers.
Export `terraform output` or read triggers in CI and apply to your ruler (Mimir/AMP/Operator) and
Alertmanager GitOps — this repo does not push rules directly to a live Prometheus API.
{% endif %}
{% elif backend == 'prometheus' %}
Deploy `prometheus/rules/` to your Prometheus ruler and sync `prometheus/alertmanager/`
via GitOps. Map receivers to **{{ notification_target }}** in your real Alertmanager config.
{% elif backend == 'datadog' %}
Import monitor JSON from `datadog/monitors/` via the Datadog API or internal GitOps.
{% endif %}

## Validate locally

Use the repave gate toolchain ([`deploy/local`](https://github.com/opsdevcode/repave/tree/main/deploy/local))
or Docker Compose for dry-run parity with CI.

```bash
yamllint .
{% if backend == 'prometheus' and output_mode == 'native' %}
promtool check rules prometheus/rules/*.yaml
amtool check-config prometheus/alertmanager/alertmanager.yaml
{% endif %}
{% if output_mode == 'terraform' %}
terraform fmt -check
terraform validate
{% endif %}
```

## Gates

Repave publish runs blueprint gates. **Dry run preview** fails (does not skip) when a required
CLI is missing — install Terraform, Conftest, promtool, and peers from the repave local deploy docs.
Terraform mode adds `terraform-fmt`, `terraform-validate`, and OPA (plan JSON or vendored fixture).

